{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789405806,"nonce":"c2EDnLl9iAp9nTdfY45C0yxkpns=","title":"String plugin: every primitive decodes the whole string it is handed","message":"`string_as_str` validates the full byte range as UTF-8 on each call, so\na primitive that reads one character or searches from an offset costs\nthe length of the string. On a 460 KB text a search per token made\n`str.split` a second slower than its own copying (fixed for `split` by\na byte-level `index_of_from`); `char_count`, `char_at`, `substring`,\n`contains`, `replace` and the rest still pay it, and a loop over a long\nstring through any of them is quadratic.\n\nFix: keep the invariant that a ZRTL string holds valid UTF-8 (every\nconstructor already checks or copies from a `\u0026str`) and read through\n`from_utf8_unchecked`, or carry a validated flag in the header; and\ngive the byte-offset primitives (`char_at_byte`, `next_byte`, `bytes`)\nthe same treatment so a cursor over a long string is constant per\nstep.","files":null}]}